---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import StatsBar from '../components/StatsBar.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout>
  <main class="pt-[72px]">
    <Hero />
    <section id="about" class="pt-md pb-lg max-w-content mx-auto px-margin-mobile md:px-margin-desktop scroll-mt-[80px]">
      <StatsBar />
      <div class="mt-lg">
        <span class="font-label text-label-sm text-primary mb-sm inline-block uppercase tracking-widest">About me</span>
        <h2 class="font-display text-display-lg-mobile md:text-display-lg font-extrabold mb-md">Who I Am</h2>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-sm">
          <p class="font-body text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
            Economics assumes humans are rational. I have met humans.
          </p>
          <p class="font-body text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
            I mean if we know what the best, most optimal decision is, why do we stray away from
            what economic theory predicts? What is the thought process?? Or what even influences the
            decision???? Having always been interested in psychology (and sometimes an occasional detour
            into neuroscience) I want to understand what goes on in people's brains when they think
            and act. This interest made me naturally gravitate towards behavioural econ and decision
            sciences. Usually, I like to think about the cognitive biases in daily life, both mine
            and my surroundings. The ideal is to explore and predict decisions under real circumstances with intention to make life
            better, efficient and equal for all.
          </p>
          <p class="font-body text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
            Going on a tangent, I am also a big fan of urban design and moving to Singapore has only
            made this interest spark more. Almost everything has been thought of so meticulously
            which is a practical application of behavioural science. From promoting good health for
            citizens (the READSG campaign) to designing intergenerational housing (Kampung Research
            Program), it proves itself worthy to why it is one of the best, if not the best cities
            to live in.
          </p>
          <p class="font-body text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
            Moving on to my background, I came into economics without knowing any math, genuinely. I
            used to think a function f(x) was f multiplied by x but my
            time at Madras School of Economics equipped me with the confidence and mental capacity
            to handle a wide range of topics such as Differential Equations, Time series methods,
            Real analysis, Stoc Proc and Applied Econometrics. On top of that, I was even chosen to be
            the TA for Mathematical Methods for Economics II and Python Programming. It wasn't easy
            at all but pushing through made me more confident in my self-efficacy and I've
            built the grit needed to survive a rigorous environment. Currently, I'm starting out at
            NUS and I'm looking forward to exploring more Behavioural econ/Decision science ideas
            during my time here.
          </p>
          <p class="font-body text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed">
            I created this site mainly to serve as a portfolio+journal where I write about things I find
            interesting so it's going to be more conversational and semi formal. For my formal work, please look at the <a href={`${base}/portfolio`} class="text-primary underline">portfolio</a> tab.
            <strong class="font-bold text-on-surface">I'm looking to work in fintech analytics or behaviour-based policy. If the role involves inference to make
            sharper, better decisions, count me in.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
